
==================================================================================================
LIMB A — source identity and absence (prereg §2)
==================================================================================================
  Held publisher text: ../bhu-reading-20260823/sources/poplawski_plb690_vor_clean.txt

  L662-664 (body):   'The mass density of a black hole also cannot exceed rho_Ce, from which
                      its minimum mass in the ECKS theory is ~10^16 kg, corresponding to
                      energy ~10^43 GeV.'
  L37-38 (abstract): 'We also estimate a maximum density of matter to be on the order of the
                      corresponding Cartan density, ~10^51 kg m^-3, which gives a lower limit
                      for black-hole masses ~10^16 kg.'
  L625-627:          'the Cartan density for an electron, rho_Ce ~ m_e/r_Ce^3 ~ 10^51 kg m^-3'

  ABSENCE CHECK: the implication is asserted TWICE ('from which', 'which gives') and the
  connecting calculation appears in NEITHER place. No intervening equation relates the density
  ceiling to a mass. Searching the full text for a mass-floor derivation returns only these
  two assertions plus the GR comparison at L668.
  => the study's premise HOLDS; K6_PREMISE_VOID does NOT fire.
C1_SOURCE_IDENTITY=PASS

==================================================================================================
Constants (control normalisations, labelled as such)
==================================================================================================
G  [SI]                                              6.6743e-11
c  [SI]                                              299792458.0
rho_Ce [kg/m^3]  (source, order of magnitude)        1e+51
claimed M_min [kg] (source, order of magnitude)      1e+16

==================================================================================================
C3 — GR benchmark: the Schwarzschild uniform mean-density identity, derived here
==================================================================================================
R_s = 2GM/c^2                                        2*G*M/c**2
V = (4/3) pi R_s^3   [EUCLIDEAN volume -- an ADDED COMPLETION] 32*pi*G**3*M**3/(3*c**6)
rho_bar = M / V                                      3*c**6/(32*pi*G**3*M**2)
prereg's stated identity 3c^6/(32 pi G^3 M^2)        3*c**6/(32*pi*G**3*M**2)
C3_GR_BENCHMARK=PASS
  (algebra only; supplies NO ECKS interior premise -- prereg §7 C3)

==================================================================================================
ROUTE B — admissible completions, each obeying the SAME ceiling rho <= rho_Ce
==================================================================================================
  Each completion below is ADMISSIBLE: entry 51 fixes neither the density measure nor the
  interior, so none is excluded by the source. All obey the same ceiling.

  A: Euclidean mean density in R_s             M_min = 2.699e+14 kg   (the most natural reading; rho_bar = 3c^6/(32 pi G^3 M^2))
  B: PROPER volume (factor 3/2 larger)         M_min = 2.204e+14 kg   (same ceiling, physical proper-volume measure instead of coordinate)

  C: LOCAL rest-frame density (the reading L629-632 actually motivates -- 'a system of
     elementary Dirac particles cannot be compressed to densities higher than the densities
     of its components'): this bounds a LOCAL quantity, not a mean. Without an interior
     profile rho(r), NO mass bound follows at all: a black hole of any mass can have local
     density below rho_Ce everywhere if its interior is not assumed uniform.
     => M_min is UNBOUNDED BELOW under completion C.

